# The composed layers that owe a sum exactly, and in which quantity. One row per (fusion, quantity)
# not suspended on any ground and not filed `derived`: the filed figure must equal the sum of the
# converted parts, less the eliminations filed against that quantity.
#
# A derived composed figure owes no equality
#   It declares itself the sum, so there is nothing filed to compare it with.
#   composition/derived_fusions.sqlc names those pairs, and they leave beside the suspensions; the
#   figure is computed in composition/derived_quantities.sqlc instead.
#
# The `quantity` column is the grain
#   Every fusion is paired with every quantity `pm.summed_quantity` declares, the whole set rather
#   than whichever quantities some layer happens to file, and the suspended pairs are removed:
#   composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc, where a ground naming no quantity has already been spread
#   over all of them. It reads that set rather than composition/suspension_grounds.sqlc. The
#   `EXCEPT` would give the same rows either way, which is exactly how repeated rows can go
#   unnoticed.
#
# The filter the composition rule turns on
#   An anti-join is a filter, and this one is the filter the whole composition rule turns on. A
#   composed figure equal to its converted parts less the elimination is not a law of the model;
#   it is an obligation a document takes on by saying it looked. This relation is the set of
#   documents that took it on, so it is the honest denominator for every claim that the composition
#   rule holds.
#
# Written as `EXCEPT`, which is what the sentence means
#   "The fusions less the suspensions", written as a `LEFT JOIN` with a NULL test, names the left
#   operand and buries the right one inside an `ON` clause. `EXCEPT` names both, in the order the
#   sentence reads, and the difference is exact here because both sides are the bare key: fusions
#   is already `SELECT DISTINCT`, and `EXCEPT` removes repeats.
#
# Not a general substitute for the anti-join
#   `composition/leaves.sqlc` carries the left row's other columns through, which `EXCEPT` cannot
#   do: it compares whole rows and returns only the columns both sides share. A difference over the
#   key alone is the case that can be written this way.
#
# A short result is not evidence on its own
#   `EXCEPT` shares precedence with `UNION` in Postgres and groups from the left, so a missing pair
#   of parentheses returns the wrong set rather than an error, and a wrong set of composed layers is
#   a perfectly ordinary table.
#
# The law is worked out, not recorded
#   algebra/owed_equality.sqlc checks on every run that these operands balance, so a number written
#   here would be a number nobody recounts. Read it there.
-- composition/fusions.sqlc for every quantity, minus the suspensions that lift each sum and the
-- composed figures filed `derived`.
SELECT f.filing, f.layer, q.quantity
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc)
) f
CROSS JOIN unnest(enum_range(NULL::pm.summed_quantity)) AS q(quantity)
EXCEPT
(
    SELECT s.composition, s.composed_layer, s.quantity
    FROM (
        :compose(composition/suspended_quantities.sqlc)
    ) s
    UNION
    SELECT d.filing, d.layer, d.quantity
    FROM (
        :compose(composition/derived_fusions.sqlc)
    ) d
)
